The owner's decision is applied, and the long-text test is decided at both seeds: when ten HotpotQA passages are compressed as one chunk, the spread layout beats the tail layout by about 25 points.

## Done this wake
- **Owner's answer applied.** You chose the seed-pooled test for "equal" (option A). "Equal" now means the 95% interval of the spread − tail difference, averaged over the two training seeds, lies within ±2 points. Each seed's own difference must also lie within ±2 points. The test is a new mode of the audit script, `scripts/spread/slice_pairs.py --pooled` (40 added lines). Its checks pass: the known reduced-budget document gain comes back at +.084 (expected +.084), and any file compared with itself gives 0.000. The campaign rules are updated, the request file is deleted and the open question is closed. Option B (a second set of 1,500 document questions) waits for the checkpoint before the retraining arm.
- **Long text as one chunk.** Accuracy is the share of correct answers as scored by the judge model, on 1,500 questions per seed. The input is about 173 compressed slots per question, at 8 tokens per slot. The uncompressed model scores .752.

| input | seed | spread ↑ | tail ↑ | spread − tail (95% CI) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| one chunk | 42 | .611 | .351 | +.260 (+.233, +.289) |
| one chunk | 43 | .616 | .369 | +.247 (+.219, +.275) |
| ten chunks | 42 | .605 | .603 | +.001 (−.021, +.025) |
| ten chunks | 43 | waiting for a re-run on today's code | .597 | — |

- **The tail layout fails on one long chunk; spread does not.** Going from ten chunks to one costs tail −.253 at seed 42 and −.229 at seed 43. It costs spread nothing (+.006 at seed 42).
- **Two new facts about the evaluation:**
  - Text answers can change when the same model is re-run on newer code: 58 of 1,500 answers changed, but the score barely moved (.603 vs .605). So text comparisons now also need both sides run on today's code.
  - The old tail photo results used a smaller image-size limit than the spread ones. This makes no difference: every photo already fits under both limits and gets the same 79,322 slots.

## Running now
All four jobs started at once, with no queue wait:
- Spread model, ten chunks, seed 43, on today's code. This closes the long-text test.
- Tail model on photos (seeds 42 and 43) and on documents (seed 43), re-run on today's code. These make the main photo and document comparisons decidable. Until then, on the older results, photos would count as "equal" (+.001) and documents are neither equal nor better (+.017).

## Next
- When the four jobs end: run the pooled test on ten chunks, which closes the long-text test, and on photos and documents.
- Then write the judge-prompt check script: re-score the same answers with a second judge prompt and confirm the one-chunk result keeps its sign.

One caveat for the checkpoint before retraining: even with both seeds pooled, 1,500 questions can call documents or text "equal" only when the true difference is about 0.1 point or less. That is the case for option B.

